{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.Mu3TargetWellPosedness","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.Mu3TargetWellPosedness","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.Mu3WellPosedness.forced_free_contrast","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.Mu3WellPosedness.forced_free_contrast","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/Mu3TargetWellPosedness.lean#L78-L88","doc":"**The forced/free contrast, packaged.**  Simultaneously, over any nontrivial\ncommutative ring: the pinned edge coefficient `μ₂` (under `M(2)=0`) misses the\nvalue `1`, while the triangle coefficient `μ₃` attains any prescribed `v`.  One\nstatement separating the structural invariant (`μ₂` forced) from the free\ncoordinate (`μ₃`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.Mu3WellPosedness.mu3_eq_A3_target_of_deuteron","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.Mu3WellPosedness.mu3_eq_A3_target_of_deuteron","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/Mu3TargetWellPosedness.lean#L70-L76","doc":"**`μ₃` collapses to the raw A=3 target when `μ₂ = 0`.**  Under the forced\ndeuteron constraint the triangle coefficient is *identically* the A=3 residual:\n`μ₃ = m₃`.  Hence the \"3-body moment\" is a coordinate name for a single isotope's\nresidual — there is no averaging and no statistical-moment method freedom. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.Mu3WellPosedness.mu3_surjective_in_target","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.Mu3WellPosedness.mu3_surjective_in_target","kind":"theorem","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/Mu3TargetWellPosedness.lean#L60-L68","doc":"**`μ₃` is FREE — a surjection onto the ring.**  With the deuteron edge target\nfixed at `m₂ = 0`, for EVERY value `v` there is an A=3 residual target `m₃` making\n`μ₃ = v` (namely `m₃ = v`).  So no structural constraint pins `μ₃`'s value: it is\na free coordinate of the residual.  (Contrast `mu2_pinned_cannot_reach_one`: the\nedge coefficient misses `1`, the triangle coefficient hits everything.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.Mu3WellPosedness.mu2_pinned_cannot_reach_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.Mu3WellPosedness.mu2_pinned_cannot_reach_one","kind":"theorem","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/Mu3TargetWellPosedness.lean#L49-L58","doc":"**`μ₂` is FORCED — it is pinned to `0` and cannot reach `1`.**  Under the\nderived deuteron self-reference `M(2) = 0`, the recovered edge coefficient is `0`\nfor EVERY choice of the A=3,4 residual targets `m₃ m₄`.  Hence there is a value\n(`1`) the pinned `μ₂` can never attain: it is genuinely constrained by structure,\nnot by fitting.  (Requires `R` nontrivial so `0 ≠ 1`.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.Mu3WellPosedness.solMu3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.Mu3WellPosedness.solMu3","kind":"def","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/Mu3TargetWellPosedness.lean#L46-L47","doc":"The A=3 (triangle) simplex coefficient: `μ₃ = m₃ − 3·m₂`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.Mu3WellPosedness.solMu2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.Mu3WellPosedness.solMu2","kind":"def","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/Mu3TargetWellPosedness.lean#L41-L44","doc":"The A=2 (edge) simplex coefficient recovered from the residual targets by the\nunit-triangular back-substitution: `μ₂ = m₂`.  Written as a function of all three\ntargets to make \"independence from the A=3,4 data\" a statement about arguments. ","signatureChunk":0}]}